Article 23

(1) The Regional Government develops cooperation patterns for the protection of women and children from violence.

(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) is in order to achieve the objectives of protecting women and children from violence in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out between the Regional Government and:

a. Central Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regional Governments;
d. Higher Education Institutions;
e. Social and Religious Institutions;
f. Non-Governmental Organizations; and/or
g. Media.
(4) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses.
