Regional Government provides legal protection as referred to in Article 6 letter b, covering:

a. providing protection in a Safe House;
b. providing legal information to victims;
c. conducting assistance for victims as witnesses from the investigation process to the verdict; and
d. providing special legal protection for child victims of acts of violence that may be carried out by appointing guardianship in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 7

(1) Regional Government conducts prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter a through empowerment and awareness raising to Families, Parents, and the Community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness raising as referred to in paragraph (1), it is implemented by means of:

a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. establishing and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. establishing networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and
g. opening an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence in every sub-district.

