Article 18

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: a. the right to be respected for their dignity and worth as human beings; b. the right to recovery;

c. the right to determine their own decisions;

d. the right to obtain information;

e. the right to confidentiality;

f. the right to social rehabilitation;

g. the right to handling of complaints in a quick, precise, comfortable manner and according to needs;

h. the right of victims and their families to receive facilitation in the judicial process;

i. the right to assistance; and

j. the right to a sense of security and protection.

